## Distinct restored finite regression

The restored checker comes from the exact `52aab147...` source blob with SHA-256
`dcab21786fc2798ab5715c353d182cdd9863685a1d8cb26531732ff9d4ff55b3`.
The only code addition rejects optimized Python, which would disable its assertions.
It checks `j=1,...,6` for both unit square and rational oblique grids with basis
`(1,0),(5/13,12/13)`: twelve complete source packets. Every pair, actual contact,
diameter, strict hull side, stopped train, crossing and endpoint multiplicity is
checked with rational arithmetic. It also bounds the displayed scalar constants
using alternating-series Machin bounds and rational square-root brackets.

For `j>=2`, each strict parallelogram hull side has length `j`, although its
subdivision contains unit boundary contacts. Such contact occurrences cannot be
counted as actual unit sides of the strict convex hull. For `j=1`, the square
attains two double-ended trains and refutes a finite depletion bound that omits
the crossing-removal error. Oblique packets have explicit same-cardinality square
competitors of smaller diameter. The checker asserts neither canonical source
hypotheses nor global optimality, disk convergence or an infinite depletion theorem.

