## Deep-port route source: complete successor comparison

Source sections 1–4 give the augmented-cell topology, actual-contact boundary
route with factor `4/sqrt(3)`, local attachment cost and exact single global
face-defect payment. Audit 134 reconstructs these arguments and the bounded-face
capsule count yielding `K_M R+B_M+5T_M`. The specified initial contact edge is
preserved by starting that route at its unloaded neighbor and appending the
edge; this adds only the stated constant.

Section 5's fixed-radius cap grid is covered by Audit 175, with its cap package
as an explicit antecedent. Homothety keeps the crop in the same cell; global
Type-II deficit controls that moving crop; boundary trimming and isoperimetry
give a quadratic coherent piece with linear grid shores. Harmonic-cell interior
disjointness identifies its actual unloaded component. The fixed radius is
chosen before taking the large-diameter limit. Audit 175's global tail theorem
also strengthens the source's conditional short-route/linear-tail alternative
to every Type-II attachment. It does not prove that tails vanish or that a cap
can be extracted from an arbitrary source.

Section 6's rational rhombus refutes boundary stretch two; Audit 134 retains
the exact example and corrected factor. Its zero-defect oblique grid and
section 6.1's thin convex polygon are already covered by the recorded route
regression and the stronger Audit 123 pinned-face family. Section 6.2's
comparison with the monotone-route source supplies no additional theorem or
closure: defect currency still needs bounded multiplicity and an actual finite
source endpoint. Section 7 correctly separates the finite fixtures from all
unbounded assertions. No source isolate is omitted or assigned core rigidity.

The restored checker has original SHA-256
`21367e572ced2b7967731ed817763717d21f7472778dd8f3f04709d217d861cc`.
Its sole addition rejects optimized Python. It checks 14 exact harmonic-fixture
augmented faces, 111 rational rhombi and 13,320 boundary pairs, 17,736 lattice
source pairs and 3,164 thin-face pairs. These independent finite fixtures were
absent from main and are useful evidence even though their analytic conclusions
